[{:seon.task/name "deps-at-the-repl"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: the :deps effect (`seon.fx/resolve-deps`) resolves a deps map through Jolt's ``jolt.deps/resolve-deps`` and answers the source roots or :seon.fx/unresolved; there is no add-lib or sync-deps at the REPL and no checksum (docs/source.md#dependencies; leaves them out). Correct, with Clojure's names (clojure.repl.deps): add-lib, add-libs and sync-deps ask the :deps effect through `my.fx/call`, load the answered roots in the agent's process and record the coordinate on its branch; a resolved jar or git tree is checked against a sha256 recorded at its first resolve, and a mismatch is the effect's typed error."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.fx-test/add-lib-loads-a-resolved-library seon.fx-test/a-changed-artifact-is-refused-by-its-checksum}}
 {:seon.task/name "an-effect-opens-a-receipt"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: an agent holds an effect only as the answer of the eval that asked, once it comes (no effect fact), so an agent that dies with a :file, :git or :model call in flight leaves no record that it asked, and a resumed branch cannot tell sent from unsent. v1 committed a receipt before the handler ran, settled it once, and never re-sent it on recovery (~/src/seon/src/seon/effect.clj). Correct: for a non-idempotent kind, the agent writes an effect fact (:seon.fx/status :open, declared then) with kind, request and the form's ordinal on its branch before `my.fx/call` sends; the answer settles that entity and links the eval; the reconciler marks a dead agent's open receipt :interrupted and never re-sends it. Foundation for `seon.fx/files-and-shell-for-any-work`."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.fx-test/a-dead-agents-open-effect-is-interrupted-not-resent seon.fx-test/an-effect-links-its-eval}}
 {:seon.task/name "files-and-shell-for-any-work"
  :seon.task/plan "Seon does any work its user wants (AGENTS §1; owner 2026-10-22). What exists: the effect kinds in resources/seon/system.edn :fx are :echo :file :source :git :deps :build :model; `seon.fx/write-file` writes any path with no prior-digest check; there is no my.fs, my.edit or my.shell. Correct: :fs (read, glob, stat, write with the prior digest as precondition), :edit (exact-span text and line windows) and :shell (argv only, cwd, an env allowlist, a stdin cap, bounded by bytes not a clock) kinds, with my.fs, my.edit and my.shell as thin wrappers over `my.fx/call`. v1's handler policy becomes config keys (:seon.config.fs/*, :seon.config.shell/env-allowlist; v1 src/seon/fs/jvm.clj, shell/jvm.clj). Each function gets a section in docs/agent.md. Deletes: write-file's unchecked path, folded into the :fs write."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.fx/an-effect-opens-a-receipt"}
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.fx-test/a-write-needs-the-prior-digest seon.fx-test/shell-answers-exit-and-digested-output seon.fx-test/shell-sees-only-allowed-env}}
 {:seon.task/name "web-fetch-and-search"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: no :web effect, so an agent cannot fetch a page or search (parity.md gap 11). v1: `my.web/fetch` and `search`, http(s) only, no userinfo in the URL, manual redirects with loop detection, a body cap (~/src/seon/src/seon/web/jvm.clj); the search key held by root, named by an env-var config key. Correct: :web-fetch and :web-search kinds in system.edn :fx, the search key read only by root's owner (as `seon.fx/model` reads the model key), with my.web as a wrapper over `my.fx/call`; caps as :seon.config.web/* keys."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.fx/an-effect-opens-a-receipt"}
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.fx-test/redirects-are-bounded seon.fx-test/search-key-stays-in-root}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-tree-run-is-one-function"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by the one-offs survey (the archived paper one-offs-2026-10-23.md (git history); owner, 2026-10-23: src resists growth so agents reuse and improve the core parts rather than making one-offs, DECISIONS). Item 5. What exists: `seon.fx/build` and `seon.fx/run-on-checkout` (the :tests effect's run, `seon.fx/run-tests`) repeat one mechanism (the `child-env-scrub` env, `bin/worktree --at`, a log file, a niced command in that tree, the cleanup). Done since: `seon.fx/test-results` reads the stored results at each test's digest (`seon.fx/stored-results`, seon.proofs' verdicts), no longer prove's stdout. Correct: one private in-tree runner both call. Risk: the two differ in where the tree lives (generations-dir against tests-dir) and in what they keep after (a build's tree stays, a test run's is removed)."
  :seon.task/kind :work}
 {:seon.task/name "the-commit-notice-commits-are-reviewed"
  :seon.task/plan "Left from seon.fx/the-standing-root-follows-main-not-the-checkouts-head (merged c5e44b3138): three commits of the commit notice reached main unreviewed (c0a9fdde89, 46c1d2929f, 10c98b1e7d), with +30 MB in `e2e calc` unexplained. The review's fixes are on main (the render proc's stale-notice skip, the conn's exception in docs/machine.md). Left: measure root at `e2e calc` now and before c0a9fdde89, find the +30 MB if it is still there, and cut what costs memory for nothing (owner, 2026-10-29: review, fix, measure)."
  :seon.task/kind :work}
]
